  "final_answer": "All four deliverables are written to `/app` and confirmed:\n\n- **`collateral_audit.csv`** \u2014 60 in-scope items, `item_id,finding` (clean = `none`).\n- **`zone_summary.csv`** \u2014 8 zones; ZN-03, ZN-07, ZN-08 are `ZONE_ALLOWANCE_BREACH`.\n- **`collateral_memo.md`** \u2014 safety-office memo per \u00a77 (date, out-of-scope+why, every flagged item with its deciding record, numbers-cleared-by-standard, zones over allowance, heightened inspection).\n- **`results.json`** \u2014 the 11 \u00a77 figures, each a JSON number.\n\nKey results (verified by two independent code paths):\n- 60 audited / 6 out of scope (`standalone_graphic`, `vehicle_wrap`).\n- **3 zones over allowance** (\u22653) \u2192 **heightened inspection in force**, tightening the \u00a74 cap by 1 sqft in those three zones (ZN-03 8\u21927, ZN-07 20\u219219, ZN-08 10\u21929), which raised 5 additional OVERSIZE findings (COL-15, COL-16, COL-42, COL-48, COL-50).\n- Figures: `collateral_count`=60, `permit_missing`=20, `egress_obstructed`=8, `oversize`=13, `compliant`=21, `flagged`=39, `finding_total`=41, `out_of_scope`=6, `pulled`=20, `zones_over_allowance`=3.\n\nOne trap worth flagging: COL-66 is `installed_signage` (not `temporary_banner`), so PMT-1013 doesn't reach it \u2014 that pulls it and keeps ZN-02 (77.5 < 80) **out** of breach, leaving exactly the three zones above.",
